<resources>
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar" >
        <item name="android:statusBarColor" >@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor" >@android:color/transparent</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Shown by the system from process start until Compose's first draw dismisses it
         (core-splashscreen's own default timing - AppActivity.onCreate() does not hold it open
         artificially, after that caused a blank splash on some fast force-kill-then-relaunch
         cycles). This is the ONLY splash Android shows - the "3b" (Reel spin-up) icon motion runs
         natively here via splash_icon_animated.xml, not as a second Compose overlay
         (SplashScreen.kt, commonMain, stays in use on iOS/Desktop/JS only, which have no
         equivalent native animated-icon API). windowSplashScreenAnimationDuration is still 850 so
         the icon plays at its intended pace on a device where first draw lands after that point;
         it may still get cut short on a faster one, but that is a better trade-off than the hold.
         The wordmark ("MyWatch"/"List" branding image) is added in values-v31/styles.xml, not
         here - windowSplashScreenBrandingImage is a real API-31+ platform SplashScreen attribute
         that androidx.core:core-splashscreen's compat theme does not expose at all below that
         level (confirmed against the library's own attrs - it only ships Background/AnimatedIcon/
         AnimationDuration/IconBackgroundColor), so this base style covers minSdk 24-30 with
         icon-only, same as before. -->
    <style name="Theme.MyWatchList.SplashBase" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_background</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon_animated</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimationDuration">850</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme</item>
    </style>

    <style name="Theme.MyWatchList.Splash" parent="Theme.MyWatchList.SplashBase" />
</resources>
